  "tldr": "One response-adaptive experiment must serve a continuum of quantiles whose precision-optimal allocations disagree. The core defines curve-wise Neyman regret from finite-population quantile scores and a maximal LIL-normalized width for an anytime QTE band, characterizes their exact nondominated frontier within marginal CDF inversion, and gives a predictable doubling-batch design and AIPW inversion band that attain every exposed point. The unrestricted minimax sharpness question remains explicit because cross-arm score dependence is not observed under two-arm randomization.",
